<article class="env-remark" id="003P">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/003P">Remark <span data-tag="003P">1.4.2.3</span>.</a> Let $S_{\bullet }$ be a simplicial set. Then the opposite simplicial set $S_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{op}}$ can be described more concretely as follows: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
For each $n \geq 0$, we have $S_{n}^{\operatorname{op}} = S_{n}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The face and degeneracy operators of $S_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{op}}$ are given by 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  (d^{n}_ i: S^{\operatorname{op}}_ n \rightarrow S^{\operatorname{op}}_{n-1}) = (d^{n}_{n-i}: S_ n \rightarrow S_{n-1}) \]
</div>
<div class="equation">
  \[  (s^{n}_ i: S^{\operatorname{op}}_ n \rightarrow S^{\operatorname{op}}_{n+1}) = (s^{n}_{n-i}: S_ n \rightarrow S_{n+1}). \]
</div>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
